{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["And the meaning of יפת is from יפה, but it is not יפה; rather it is like ירחיב (Deuteronomy 12:20), and in Aramaic similarly, and it is of the heavy added binyan like ומלכים יַרד (Isaiah 41:2). And in this verse, may YHWH enlarge Japheth — also HaShem — for the meaning of וישכון באהלי שם is that Elohim will dwell in the tents of Shem, for in the first verse HaShem blessed [saying] so:" "<b>And Canaan shall be a servant to them.</b> To Shem and to Japheth and also to their brothers, and he is an everlasting servant, for from these the whole earth was scattered, and this matter was after many years after the flood."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "Resolved השם / ד׳ uniformly as HaShem per divine-name rules. The referent of 'the first verse' is the blessing in the preceding verse (Genesis 9:26)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:02.950112693Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}